A watch signals the bits it is set with, not those of them the capability it was set with may signal,
so a thread's faults speak for bits its watcher was never given;
a thread's watch is derived from its capability, with no more bits.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: slot is not derived from its parent

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -459,7 +459,6 @@ static int op_thread(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, uint3
             if (err != KERR_OK) {
                 return err;
             }
-            bits &= nc.b;
             if (bits == 0) {
                 return KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
             }
